# Polygenic hierarchies of macroscale brain structural organisation: analysis code

Code and small input/intermediate data for the main figures and supplementary analyses of
"Polygenic hierarchies of macroscale brain structural organisation".

Related repositories:
- Imaging phenotype generation (parcellation of cortical measures): https://github.com/ucam-department-of-psychiatry/UKB
- GWAS, LDSC, HyPrColoc, FLAMES and MAGMA were run outside this repository with their standard tools; their outputs are the inputs here.

<!-- Add the journal-required statement on AI-assisted code development here, if applicable. -->

## How to run

1. Clone the repository and `setwd()` to its root (or set the environment variable `GWAS_MRI_DIR`).
2. Install the packages in `R_packages.txt`.
3. Run a script from the root, e.g. `source("scripts/02_genetic_clustering/Final_Figure2_script.R")`.

Every script starts with `source("config.R")`, which defines `proj_dir`. Inputs are read from `Data/`, results are
written to `Outputs/`. Some scripts are slow (spin tests use 10,000 rotations; enrichment models use permutations)
and a few need data that is too large for GitHub (see `DATA.md`).

## Scripts and manuscript items

| Script | Manuscript item |
|---|---|
| `01_genome_wide_results/Final_Figure1_script.R` | Figure 1 |
| `02_genetic_clustering/Final_Figure2_script.R` | Figure 2 |
| `02_genetic_clustering/Final_leiden_searchscript.R` | Figure 2: Leiden clustering across random seeds |
| `02_genetic_clustering/Standalone_UMAP_parametersweepscript.R` | Figure 2: UMAP n_neighbors / min_dist sweep |
| `02_genetic_clustering/Supplementary_FIgure1script.R` | Supplementary Figure 2 (clustering after pruning correlated IDPs) |
| `02_genetic_clustering/Final_extendedFigure3_script.R` | Supplementary Figure 4A, Extended Data Figure 4B-C |
| `03_genes_celltypes_GO/Final_Figure4_script.R` | Figure 3 and Supplementary Figure 5 (FLAMES genes, cell types, GO, family similarity) |
| `03_genes_celltypes_GO/Siletti_FLAMES_enrichment.R` | Supplementary Figure 6 (adult brain cell types) |
| `03_genes_celltypes_GO/Final_Figure5_TFenrichement_script.R` | Supplementary Figure 7 (TF / eRegulon analyses) |
| `03_genes_celltypes_GO/emVAR_FLAMES_geneprioritisationcomparison.R` | Results: emVar / ABC concordance with FLAMES |
| `03_genes_celltypes_GO/FLAMES_paneloverlap.R` | Results: clinical gene panels |
| `04_cortical_gPCs/Final_ExtDataFig4_PCA_master.R` | Figure 4, Supplementary Tables 8-10 (gPCs, spin tests) |
| `04_cortical_gPCs/Final_ExtDataFig5_assembly.R` | Figure 4, Supplementary Figure 8 |
| `04_cortical_gPCs/Final_SuppFig9_median_PC_correspondence.R` | Supplementary Figure 9 |
| `05_arealisation/Final_Figure6_arealizationscript.R` | Figure 5 pipeline and Supplementary Tables 10-13 |
| `05_arealisation/Final_Figure6_full_and_GRNsupp.R` | Figure 5 (final layout), Supplementary Figure 10 |
| `05_arealisation/Arealisation_leadSNP_LD_check.R` | Lead SNP per arealisation gene (needs `LDLINK_TOKEN`) |
| `05_arealisation/Arealisation_Script2_by_measure.R` | Extracts lead-SNP betas across parcels (cluster; set `SUMSTAT_DIR`) |
| `05_arealisation/Arealisation_beta_hitparcel_validation.R` | Beta QC: Wilcoxon and distance-decay spin test |
| `06_novel_loci/*` | Comparison with previously reported loci (liftover, positions, PLINK2 clumping) |

Some script names reflect earlier figure numbering (for example `Final_Figure4_script.R` produces Figure 3 and
`Final_Figure6_*` produce Figure 5). The header of each script says which item it feeds.

## Order of use

1. Clustering scripts need only `Data/rg_matrix.rds`.
2. `Final_Figure4_script.R` builds the FLAMES figure from `Data/FLAMES_gene_prioritisation_results.txt`.
3. `Final_Figure6_arealizationscript.R` builds the arealisation tables first; the lead-SNP, beta extraction and
   validation scripts then extend them (the extraction step runs on the cluster).
4. `Final_ExtDataFig4_PCA_master.R` first, then `Final_ExtDataFig5_assembly.R` and the supplements.

Intermediate tables that later steps read are included under `Outputs/` so each stage can be run on its own.

## Things to know

- `Data/FLAMES_gene_prioritisation_results.txt` is Supplementary Table 4 with the column names the scripts expect.
- `Data/rg_matrix.rds` is the 2,326 x 2,326 LDSC genetic correlation matrix.
- Some retained scripts still contain sensitivity branches that exclude a set of phenotypes ("outliers"); the
  manuscript does not report these.
- Not in this repository: the LDSC, HyPrColoc (Supplementary Figure 3) and FLAMES runs themselves, and a single
  script from PLINK clumps to the final novel-locus counts.
- Figure 1C is computed from `Data/UKB_sig_info.txt` without a significance filter, so it reports genome-wide
  (P <= 5e-8) concordance; the experiment-wide concordance quoted in the text uses P <= 4.65e-11.

Important Folder Description:

1. genetic_data = imputated genotype data -> filtered imputated SNP data.
2. imaging_data = MRI microstructure and macrostructure data -> filtered MRI data with selected individuals
